16.139.m:
The righteous-minded [Citra] worshipped him with incenses, garlands, and ointments;
and with the sixty-eight names declared by Vasiṣṭha,
he praised the lord, the god of gods, Sūrya, with palms joined. (8)

I shall praise him who is endowed with secret names:
Muṇḍīrasvāmin in the morning at the confluence of the Gaṅgā and the ocean;
Kālapriya at midday, resting upon the bank of the Yamunā; (11)
